% M3-T2: the reifier decided BY SEARCH, not by a row -- which is the only state in
% which the reifier's literal is load-bearing in a trace line.
%
% Every other reified model in this directory settles its reifier at level 0, from a
% clause or a unit row, and then `~b_ge_1` is derivable by unit propagation on its own:
% a reason that dropped the reifier's fact would still produce a rup veripb accepts.
% Measured, and the reason this model exists (see the M3-T2 report): dropping it
% reddens NOTHING without this file and reddens this file with it.
%
% b <-> (x = y) and b <-> (x <> y) at once is unsatisfiable, and nothing about it is
% visible to bounds propagation at level 0: with x and y both open on [0, 1], neither
% reification's entailment piece can fire, so first-fail's declaration-order tiebreak
% branches on b and every conflict below sits under that decision. Widths are 2.
var bool: b :: output_var;
var 0..1: x :: output_var;
var 0..1: y :: output_var;
constraint int_eq_reif(x, y, b);
constraint int_ne_reif(x, y, b);
solve satisfy;
